{
  "why": "The typed-operation fault record (`semio.typed-operation-fault.v1`, `🧬️schema/🧯️typed-operation-fault/🔣️.json`), written once and read by two implementations: the Rust law `app::typed_operation_fault_tests` drives `TypedOperationFault::of_fault`/`encode`/`decode`, and the AJV twin (`🧪️tests/🧯️typed-operation-fault/🟦️.ts`) validates every expected record against the schema and drives the host decoder `decodeTypedOperationFaultV1`. `records` states what one `Fault` becomes: a frozen code is non-empty and at most `limits.codeBytes` UTF-8 bytes, else the record answers `limits.untypedCode`; the message is clipped to `limits.messageBytes` UTF-8 bytes on a character boundary; the parameters (added as `Fault::with_parameter` adds them: at most `limits.parameters`, each value clipped to `limits.parameterValueBytes` UTF-8 bytes on a character boundary, control characters as spaces) ride along; the encoded record fits one result page (`limits.pageBytes`). `decodes` states which byte strings are a record: only an object of exactly the schema's five members, of this schema, with a frozen code, a known origin, a bounded message and at most `limits.parameters` well-formed, bounded parameters; framed text (`<code>\\u001f<message>`) and prose are not. `…Repeat` spells a long string as `text` repeated `count` times.",
  "limits": {
    "codeBytes": 64,
    "messageBytes": 256,
    "pageBytes": 4096,
    "untypedCode": "interactive-job.app-owned-output",
    "parameters": 8,
    "parameterNameBytes": 32,
    "parameterValueBytes": 64
  },
